Beneath a Typographic Sky
=========================

A modified version of Beneath a Steel Sky, drawn in the terminal.

Beneath a Steel Sky (C) Revolution Software Ltd 1993-. All game content
(art, story, characters, speech, music) is Revolution's. Revolution
released the game as freeware in 2003; its licence (readme.txt, shipped
beside the game data) allows free distribution and modified versions
marked as such. This is one: the game's pictures are redrawn as text
characters and its text is set in the terminal's own type. The game data
itself is unmodified. This version is free and is never sold.

The engine is a Rust port of the ScummVM sky engine (engines/sky,
(C) The ScummVM Team, GPL-3.0-or-later), and is itself
GPL-3.0-or-later. The AdLib music is emulated with nuked-opl3, a port of
Nuked-OPL3 by Nuke.YKT (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

